    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Remove deprecation for navigator.vendor and navigator.platform]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27342</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27342"/>
        <updated>2025-08-14T00:33:18.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177243?u=702b96ad69bf6e6823b7530dad917ab8b4d9b761&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">The WhatWG spec for <a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#the-navigator-object" rel="nofollow">the navigator object</a> does not list these properties as deprecated, but <em>does</em> call them out as being <em>useful</em> rather than to be avoided.</p>
<p dir="auto">While for security reasons the <em>amount</em> of information provided by browsers through navigator properties has been reduced from what the older standard allowed for (as highlighted by the warning in the spec that "<em>user agent implementers are strongly urged to include as little information in this API as possible</em>", which all browsers have indeed taken to heart by only providing summary information rather than detailed information), the properties themselves have not been deprecated, and the use of <code class="notranslate">navigator</code> has in no way been marked as bad. As per the text for the navigator object itself, rather the opposite:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">In certain cases, despite the best efforts of the entire industry, web browsers have bugs and limitations that web authors are forced to work around.</p>
<p dir="auto">This section defines a collection of attributes that can be used to determine, from script, the kind of user agent in use, in order to work around these issues.</p>
</blockquote>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#the-navigator-object" rel="nofollow">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#the-navigator-object</a></li>
<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-vendor-dev" rel="nofollow">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-vendor-dev</a></li>
<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-platform-dev" rel="nofollow">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-platform-dev</a></li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1336781702" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/17322" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/17322/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/17322">#17322</a> (which incorrectly marked them as deprecated in 2022, when the spec already read what it reads today)</li>
<li><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1184851631" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/14429" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/14429/hovercard?comment_id=3092444674&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/14429#issuecomment-3092444674">mdn/content#14429 (comment)</a> (link to a summary comment that tracks how this change happened, and how it probably shouldn't have)</li>
</ul>]]></content>
